  "body": "## What\n\nImplement the D1-040 design: a `documents`/`document` ClientFrame/ServerFrame pair in the world-session protocol, modelled on `records`, so web and CLI clients can read the public documents — today reachable only from the SSH shell, which reads the shared server blob store directly. Scope is server-wide parity (the design's Decision 1): the frames expose exactly the set SSH exposes today; per-world scoping waits on the deferred per-world document store and is out of scope here.\n\n## Design\n\n`doc/2026-11-01T16-05-00Z_design_documents_session_frames/2026-11-01T16-05-00Z_design_documents_session_frames.md` (lands with PR #3760; tracker #535 item D1-040). The design is decided — frame shapes, authorization, bounds, the serving-logic move, and test expectations are all pinned there. Read it first; this issue is the delivery vehicle, not a second design pass.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `ClientFrame::Documents { capability, prefix, after }` and `ClientFrame::Document { capability, name }` in `pkgs/id/src/world_session/types.rs`; `ServerFrame::Documents { names, next_after }` and `ServerFrame::Document { name, size, text }` per the design (no `sequence` on the list frame — the design records why)\n- [ ] Serving logic (`list_public_documents` / `read_public_document` and their name/bounds rules) lives in the session layer next to `records_session`; authorization is the records rule (join capability → `participant_id`, else `join denied`); the design's one structural unknown — how the session layer reaches the blob store the SSH shell holds today — is resolved and noted on this issue\n- [ ] SSH shell is frame-backed: `command_frame` gains `documents` / `documents_continue` / `document` arms mirroring `records`; rendered SSH output (`public named files:` listing, `[listing truncated]`, `--- {name} ({size} bytes; read-only) ---` header, `/help`) is byte-identical to before\n- [ ] Contract updated on both sides: frames named in `pkgs/id/src/shell_contract` and the shared frame contract; web contract tests extended; web client gains the minimal list + read documents panel the design specifies\n- [ ] Tests per the design's test expectations: session tests mirroring `records_session` (paging, prefix, `after` exclusivity, oversized/non-viewable/missing refusals, `join denied`), contract accept/refuse cases, existing SSH document shell tests passing against the frame-backed path\n- [ ] Existing mcpx/id CI green in GitHub Actions on the PR (note: pkgs/mcpx conformance has a pre-existing compile break on main — features_test.go:308 — do not chase it here)\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Document writes/publishing (unchanged), a `documents_ticket` replication frame (design non-goal), any change to which documents are public (#548 owns the store).\n\n## Links\n\n- Tracker: #535 (D1-040). Design PR: #3760. Prerequisite: #548 (closed).\n- Model: `records` frames in `pkgs/id/src/world_session/types.rs`, `records_session` in `pkgs/id/src/world_session/mod.rs`.\n\n",
